 ## Background
-TriplaneGaussian was proposed as a method to generate 3DGS from a single image using a hybrid representation of tri-plane and 3DGS [S1]. It was introduced in the context of recent advances in 3D Gaussian Splatting, aiming to leverage existing 3D datasets and large models for direct generation [S1]. It is cited alongside other generative methods like LGM, AGG, BrightDreamer, GRM, IM-3D, and Gamba [S1].
+TriplaneGaussian was proposed in the context of recent advances in 3D Gaussian Splatting [S1]. It is cited as a method that explores utilizing existing 3D datasets and constructing large models to directly generate 3DGS representation from a single image [S1]. It is distinct from methods like LGM, which uses multi-view images, and BrightDreamer, which predicts deviations from fixed anchor points [S1].
 
